{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C", "description": "This file contains unit tests for parsing trailer headers in commit messages or similar text blocks. It defines multiple test functions that validate the behavior of a trailer iterator implementation, ensuring proper extraction and handling of key-value trailer lines, including edge cases like no input, no newline start, presence of body text, multiple trailer blocks, and non-trailer lines.", "external_files": ["unit-test.h", "trailer.h"], "external_methods": ["trailer_iterator_init", "trailer_iterator_advance", "trailer_iterator_release", "cl_assert_equal_s", "cl_assert_equal_i"], "published": [], "classes": [], "methods": [{"name": "void t_trailer_iterator(const char * msg,size_t num_expected,struct contents * contents)", "description": "Helper function to initialize a trailer iterator, advance through trailer lines, and perform assertions to verify line contents against expected data.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "void test_trailer__empty_input(void)", "description": "Test case for empty input string.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "void test_trailer__no_newline_start(void)", "description": "Test case where the input trailer lines start immediately without a preceding newline.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "void test_trailer__newline_start(void)", "description": "Test case with trailer lines starting after an initial newline.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "void test_trailer__no_body_text(void)", "description": "Test case with trailer lines following a message subject with no intervening body text.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "void test_trailer__body_text_no_divider(void)", "description": "Test case with a message body containing multiple trailer lines after some text and special characters.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "void test_trailer__body_no_divider_2nd_block(void)", "description": "Test case with multiple trailer blocks, where l